per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.prop-mobius-nogo"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.prop-mobius-nogo"],"id":"long.prop-mobius-nogo","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Proposition 10.10 (Möbius-support countermodel: the natural negative-sign candidate overshoots)","locator":"Long record Proposition 10.10, p. 118, label prop:mobius-nogo","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*The signed Lambert identity $\\sum_{d\\ge1}\\mu(d)/(2^d-1) = 1/2$ is exact. Writing $N:=\\{d:\\mu(d)=-1\\}$: $\\sum_{d\\in N}1/(2^d-1) = 1/2 + \\sum_{d\\in P}1/(2^d-1)$ where $P:=\\{d\\ge2:\n\\mu(d)=1\\}$, and quantitatively $1/2 + 1/63 \\le \\sum_{d\\in N}1/(2^d-1)$ (using the first positive tail term $d=6$, $\\mu(6)=1$) ; the negative-Möbius support strictly *overshoots* $1/2$ by at least $1/63$.*\n\n***Scope.** Rules out exactly one natural candidate infinite Boolean support (the negative-Möbius set) as a witness for $1/2\\in\\mathcal A$. A route-sufficiency no-go only ; it says nothing about whether *some other* infinite Boolean support sums to $1/2$. **Object or representation:** about the *object* ; a genuine value inequality for one specific candidate set, not a coordinate artifact. Margin $1/63$ is the concrete number any repair attempt (adding/removing finitely many elements) must close or exceed.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.prop-mobius-nogo","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.prop-mobius-nogo","id":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.prop-mobius-nogo%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_first_positiveMobius_tail_term%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.prop-mobius-nogo%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_first_positiveMobius_tail_term%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_first_positiveMobius_tail_term"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.prop-mobius-nogo","id":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.prop-mobius-nogo%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_mobius_support_overshoots_half%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.prop-mobius-nogo%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_mobius_support_overshoots_half%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_mobius_support_overshoots_half"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/evidence/mapping.long.prop-mobius-nogo","id":"field:209f0889640902a77567767abb37c69be13e248481bc91748e0a896dc8b353f9","kind":"subject_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/evidence/mapping.long.prop-mobius-nogo","semantic_class":"provenance_field_reference","source_field":"subject_ids","to":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.prop-mobius-nogo"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.prop-mobius-nogo","id":"field:4312c2d3e900c7dc0904c818a5776a841aeb0563c1f67271b0fc1786daecb490","kind":"evidence_ids","